comments.body:
There are a few noisy `util::NotNull{std::make_unique<T>(...)}` usages here (`dbwrapper.cpp`, `net.cpp` (×2), `txmempool.h`), in a follow-up we could add a `util::MakeNotNullUnique`:
```C++
/// Like std::make_unique, but returns a NotNullUniquePtr.
template <typename T, typename... Args>
NotNullUniquePtr<T> MakeNotNullUnique(Args&&... args)
{
    return NotNull{std::make_unique<T>(std::forward<Args>(args)...)};
}
```

nit: unrelated, but since we're touching `CreateNewBlock`, we could also avoid the naked `new` here:
```diff
-    pblocktemplate.reset(new CBlockTemplate());
+    pblocktemplate = std::make_unique<CBlockTemplate>();
```

